Range: 60 feet
Target: One creature, object, location, shrine, corpse, vessel, spirit trace, or visible manifestation
Duration: Instantaneous
Cost: 0 CP
You listen for the Nature of a spirit or spiritual presence.
Choose one target within range that you can perceive. You learn whether it is:
- a spirit;
- possessed or hosted by a spirit;
- carrying a bound spirit;
- marked by a spirit;
- haunted;
- spiritually inhabited;
- spiritually empty where it should not be;
- a vessel, shrine, anchor, offering site, or spirit trail.
If the target is a spirit or contains a spirit, you learn one of the following:
- one Nature Tag;
- whether the spirit is willing, hostile, afraid, hungry, bound, sleeping, or hidden;
- whether the spirit has a visible Need or Offering;
- whether a Binding Seal or Hosting Bond is present;
- whether the spirit is weaker, similar, or stronger than you in rough cultivation pressure;
- whether the spirit's Nature is safe, dangerous, corrupted, sacred, daemonic, ancestral, bestial, local, or alien.
If you use Read the Spirit Nature as an Action, learn two pieces of information instead of one. You may also ask the GM one practical question about interacting with the spirit.
Examples:
- What offering would make it listen?
- What taboo should I avoid?
- Is this spirit trapped or willingly present?
- What is the safest way to speak to it?
- What kind of vessel holds it?
- Which of its Nature Tags is most active right now?
- Is this a companion, prisoner, parasite, or invader?
Read the Spirit Nature does not force the spirit to answer, reveal its true name, or submit to you.
### Spirit Regard
When you successfully Read the Spirit Nature, you may place a Spirit Regard on the target.
Spirit Regard lasts for 1 hour, until you dismiss it, until the target is no longer on the same plane or layer of reality, or until the target hides its Nature with a stronger effect.
You have Advantage on the next Charisma, Wisdom, or Cultivation Check you make to communicate with, soothe, bargain with, bind, host, exorcise, or command a target bearing your Spirit Regard.
You may maintain a number of Spirit Regards equal to your Proficiency Bonus.
