talents.full_description:
Classification: Secret Fate Inheritance
Prerequisite: CL 17+, Fate-Sovereign Incarnation, hidden forbidden ledger scripture
Action Type: Reaction
Factory Combat Bucket: reaction
Factory Routing: combat_action_row
Trigger: A creature within 60 feet would fail a roll, suffer a critical hit, be reduced to 0 HP, or be caught in an immediate calamity
Cost: 15 CP
Use Limit: Once per week
You write one correction into the margin of Heaven’s ledger.
Choose one immediate, narrow, plausible alternative:
turn one failed roll into a successful roll;
turn one successful roll into a failed roll;
turn one critical hit into a normal hit or normal miss;
cause one creature reduced to 0 HP to remain at 1 HP;
cause one destroyed ordinary object to remain intact at 1 HP;
cause one attack targeting an ally to strike an unattended nearby object instead;
place one creature in an adjacent safe space instead of inside a collapsing hazard.
The correction must be narrow, immediate, plausible, and limited to one triggering event.
Ink Brush That Corrects Heaven cannot:
revive the dead;
restore spent CP or Stamina;
undo an entire encounter;
erase a completed turn;
restore an expended Legendary or Secret technique;
create an impossible object or ally;
remove permanent cultivation consequences;
cancel a Heavenly Tribulation unless the tribulation rules explicitly allow it;
overturn a divine decree without GM permission.
After using this Secret Inheritance, gain 3 Heaven’s Notice. The next time you undergo a breakthrough or tribulation, the GM may treat this correction as an unresolved debt.

