talents.full_description:
Prerequisite: Script-Sealed Mechanist, Magic Trigger, CL 10+
When you set Activation Trap, spend the CP cost of one compatible technique you know and store that technique inside the trap.
The technique must:
have an activation time of one Action or Bonus Action;
target one creature or create an area with a legal point of origin;
have an instantaneous duration or Concentration duration no longer than 1 minute;
be approved by the GM as physically and metaphysically compatible with a prepared trigger.
When the trap triggers, release the technique from the trap’s space.
If the technique requires Concentration, you begin Concentrating when the trap triggers. If you cannot Concentrate at that moment, the technique fails.
A trap can store only one technique through Scripted Release.

When you use Ruin Channel on an unarmed strike, fist, palm, claw, spear-hand, or other Internal Channel, increase the Ruin Channel bonus damage by 1d8.
If the attack hits a creature, choose one:
- the target cannot regain HP until the start of your next turn;
- the target has Disadvantage on the next Constitution saving throw it makes before the end of its next turn;
- the target cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.
After resolving the attack, gain 1 Black Vein Strain.

You may use needles, darts, hairpins, bone spikes, or similar Tiny piercing implements as External Channels for Ruin Channel.
When you hit with a Ruin Needle attack, choose one:
- the target cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn;
- the target cannot regain CP until the start of your next turn;
- the target has Disadvantage on the next check made to maintain a stance, form, or ongoing technique before the end of its next turn.
The needle gains 1 Crack and is usually destroyed after the attack.

**Prerequisite:** CL 15+, Hollowing Field
**Action Type:** Action
**Range:** Self
**Area:** 60-foot emanation
**Duration:** Concentration, up to 1 minute
**Cost:** 4 CP
You become the center of a collapsing agreement.
For the duration:
- hostile creatures in the area cannot regain HP on the same turn they take Ruin damage from you;
- temporary qi structures, summoned constructs, barriers, wards, and non-Secret defensive effects in the area take Ruin damage equal to your Cultivation Level at the start of each of your turns;
- once per turn, when you deal Ruin damage to a creature in the area, add 4d10 Ruin damage;
- when a hostile creature in the area casts, activates, or sustains a technique with Concentration or an equivalent state, it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take Ruin damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus d10.
At the end of each of your turns while the domain persists, suffer one cost:
- gain 2 Black Vein Strain;
- take Ruin self-damage equal to 5d6 + your Proficiency Bonus;
- destroy one non-artifact External Channel you are carrying;
- reduce your current and maximum HP by 10 until you finish a Long Rest.
If the domain ends because your Concentration breaks, suffer Ruin Backlash twice.

